WEBVTT

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:11.990
Please don't expect too much from it.
This story is a simple illustration of the three
Minami sisters and the ordinary life they lead.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.700
Man, we sure made the most
of this year's summer too.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.080
Yeah.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.080
We did a ton of stuff.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.500
But...

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.750
I didn't get to go to the beach.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.340
Do I hear regret in your voice?

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:32.510
You can't say you've made the most of your summer if you have any regrets.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:33.380
All right.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.140
Let's hit the beach!

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.730
Wh-Why'd you put this on me?!

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.360
Well, it's too late to hit the beach now.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.650
But we can simulate the feeling.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.400
Didn't you have any others?!

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.240
What's with all these frills?!

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.320
It's cute.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.860
Listen to me!

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:57.160
All right.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.580
That's one regret down.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.660
Any others?

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.790
Here! I've got one!

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:04.870
Oh? What is it?

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.670
I want to go on a trip with a sleepover!

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.750
A trip <i>does</i> sound good.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:12.130
Let's go on a trip.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:14.470
Can we, Kana-chan?
Woohoo!
Yeah!

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:16.630
What's all the fuss about?

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:19.640
Hey, Touma! Why are you in my swimsuit?!

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:24.520
All right! Everyone go home, get packed, and come back here ready for a trip!

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.980
Yeah!

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:00.030
Coming for a Late Summer Visit

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.870
It's hot...

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.170
It's really hot...

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:18.760
Did you enjoy your two-day, one-night trip to the Minami household, madame?

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.930
Kana-chan, this wasn't a trip.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.220
It was just a sleepover.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:22.930
Right? Right?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.680
Hey, keep it down.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:26.430
Oh, you're awake too, Chiaki?

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.310
How could I sleep? You're
.making way too much noise.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:30.810
But it's hot!

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.600
And it's not a trip!

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:38.190
Then would you like to experience our ghost-story service on this hot and stuffy night, madame?

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:41.400
How about your air-conditioner service on this hot and stuffy night?

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.030
I'm afraid we don't offer that, madame.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.120
The service here stinks!

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.290
We don't need any ghost stories.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.580
Get to sleep.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.830
Sure you're not just scared?

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.370
I'm <i>not</i> scared!

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:56.000
Let's do it. Let's all tell ghost stories.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.210
Hold on a minute.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.800
What is it, Chiaki?

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.310
You're participating too, Haruka-neesama.

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:09.520
I knew it. You <i>are</i> scared.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.230
What now, Kana?

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.980
We're telling ghost stories.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.190
Okay, let's start with Uchida.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.730
Huh? Me?

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.570
Um...

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:22.280
Oh!

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.490
Once upon a time, in a land far away...

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.280
That's a fairy tale!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:30.370
You think you can scare me with a lousy ghost story like that?!

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.790
What? Uh... Sorry?

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:33.620
You're next, Touma.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.960
Me?

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.080
Uh...

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.090
Then...

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.420
The Demonic Refrigerator,

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.260
The Devil's Washing Machine,

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.630
or The Dreadful Vacuum Cleaner.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.220
Which do you want?

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.550
Trying to inspire fear in us with typical household objects?

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:51.390
And you're giving us three choices? Clever.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:54.140
So we choose a household appliance?

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:55.900
I'll take the vacuum cleaner.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.060
Wait, Kana? You want the vacuum cleaner?

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.480
You sure you want the vacuum cleaner?

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:00.440
All right.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.980
The Dreadful Vacuum Cleaner.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.530
Okay.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.160
Huh?

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.700
How'd the story go again?

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:08.870
You forgot it?!

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.040
You built all that up just to let us down?

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.910
All you've got are the titles!

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.660
Huh? You were scared of the titles?

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.830
Oh, I know that story.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:18.250
What?

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:18.670
All right. It's in your hands, Uchida.

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:20.750
No need to force yourself.
All right. It's in your hands, Uchida.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.130
It's gotten pretty late, you know.
You got it!

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:30.220
The Dreadful Vacuum Cleaner.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.560
There once lived a newlywed couple.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:37.400
One day, they bought a new vacuum cleaner for their apartment.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.940
But that night...

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.360
My wife.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.570
My newlywed wife.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:44.820
Ah, my wife.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.070
What is it, my newlywed husband?

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:51.990
What kind of vacuum cleaner is the vacuum cleaner we bought today?

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:54.540
I cannot hold back my curiosity.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.500
The vacuum cleaner we bought today?

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.290
I hope you won't regret asking that question.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.000
I won't.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:05.210
Really?

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:06.880
Really.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.140
Then I will explain.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:14.020
The vacuum cleaner we bought today...

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:15.810
is...

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.640
full of bread.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:24.070
We bought a vacuum cleaner full of bread today?

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:27.650
Bread-full vacuum cleaner...

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:33.370
A bread-full vacuum cleaner.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.620
It was just a horrible joke!

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:40.210
You got it mixed it up with the story of The Dreadful Miso Soup.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.710
You mean the one with the "head-full" pun?

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:46.210
What happened to the ghost story?

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:46.960
Huh?

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.180
Then how did the story go?

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.510
I remember!

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.770
They got the vacuum cleaner from someone.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:56.930
Really?

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.520
Oh, that story?

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.100
Didn't the moaning come
from the vacuum cleaner?

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.440
She just spoiled the big twist!

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.690
Wasn't there some other big twist?

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:07.110
No, the moaning was the twist.

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.400
Wasn't it a middle-aged couple in that one?

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.320
We just can't get our stories straight.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:16.620
What?

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.790
Moaning? Where's it coming from?

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:23.250
They say ghosts come
when you talk about them.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.380
Quit it!

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.050
Don't tell me it's our vacuum cleaner!

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.220
What the heck, Haruka?!

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.680
Don't scare us like that!

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.260
Stop it!

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:38.770
That surprised me.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:39.810
Huh?

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.310
Oh, it was just a dream?

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:43.270
Thank goodness...

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:46.440
So that moaning was coming from Haruka?

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.650
What kind of nightmare did you have?

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.240
Well, it was really scary.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.160
Something heavy was...

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.200
What happened again?

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:01.710
That's enough ghost stories!

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.380
Let's talk about the
types of guys we're into!

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:06.170
We can't do that, Kana!

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:08.460
So, who's first?

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.050
Let's go oldest first!

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:11.300
Yeah!

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:12.880
I agree!

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.180
It's all yours, Haruka.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:17.430
Huh?

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:31.400
It's the start of second term,
but it's still so hot!

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.780
Summer sure is long this year.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.780
Good morning!

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:37.870
What's up with you guys?

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:41.290
It's a new term!
Where's your energy?!

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.290
Kana...

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.540
How can <i>you</i> have so
much energy in this heat?

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:46.540
Huh?

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:59.510
This morning, I ate breakfast with my left hand and put my shoes on the wrong feet to distract myself...

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:02.520
And I'd finally managed to
forget about the heat, too!

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.900
Then the heat that I'd forgotten attacked me all at once.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.520
It's so hot!

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.820
One of you needs to take responsibility for this and cool me off.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.990
Kana, I'll buy you a popsicle
on the way home.

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:18.030
Keiko, you shouldn't spoil her like that.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:20.030
A popsicle?

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.620
Oh, right.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:25.580
I got a winning stick yesterday.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.960
So you get to cool down for free. Isn't that good enough?

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:30.090
Well, you see...

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:34.050
I've got a bit of a toothache,
so I can't eat popsicles.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:41.220
I remember now... I have a toothache.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:42.350
You can have it.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.140
Huh?

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:50.060
I'd be too embarrassed
to redeem it, for one...

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:50.940
Huh?

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.980
I'm trying to cut down on
..sugary things right now...

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.660
My stomach's a bit upset right now.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:01.620
I got one too!

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.620
What should we do with this winning stick?

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.700
I guess we'll have to give it back to Kana.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:10.960
You look a lot better, Kana.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:12.250
What?

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.510
She forgot all about the pain and heat.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:16.720
Winner

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.760
Thanks for giving this to
us, but we can't take it.
Winner

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.140
Huh?

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.850
Oh. She remembered again.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:27.980
It hurts.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.150
It's hot.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:33.020
I guess I'll just have to put it away until my tooth feels better.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.280
The summer grasses—

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.570
For many brave warriors,

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:39.320
The aftermath of dreams.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.280
Kana.

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:42.120
Hey, no plagiarism.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:46.250
But you can tell it's mine, right?

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:50.170
Huh?

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:52.920
How many counts of plagiarism does that make?

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.210
No...

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:56.130
I got this winning stick last year.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:59.880
Seems you only cared enough to put it away and forget about it.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:07.470
It hurts...

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.730
Presents from Kana?

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:12.310
Thanks.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:14.360
It hurts...

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:16.320
You'd better go to the dentist soon.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.080
Sensei.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.370
We can't do this, Sannomiya-kun.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:36.710
Sensei!

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:37.710
Sannomiya-kun...

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.050
Sensei...

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:41.430
N-Ninomiya-kun?!
Uncle Takeru's drinking beer.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:42.720
Uncle Takeru's drinking beer.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.390
My dad told me that beer's
really good on hot days.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:46.760
Sensei!
My dad told me that beer's
really good on hot days.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:48.270
Ninomiya-kun...

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:48.560
But it's bitter, isn't it?

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:49.230
Sensei!
But it's bitter, isn't it?

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:50.180
Sanno—Ninomiya-kun?!
But it's bitter, isn't it?

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:50.940
It's bitter, but it tastes good?

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:52.310
Ninomiya-kun!
It's bitter, but it tastes good?

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:53.850
Uchida, you can't drink until you're 20.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:54.980
Sensei...
Uchida, you can't drink until you're 20.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:55.610
Uchida, you can't drink until you're 20.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:55.690
I know that.
Uchida, you can't drink until you're 20.

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:56.900
I know that.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:12:00.690
Kana, could you take
these to Uncle Takeru?

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.200
Green soybeans?

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.740
Got some for me too?

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.660
If not, I'll just help myself to a few.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.660
Kana!

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:11.000
Wh-Why'd you hit me?

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:14.420
Is taking a few beans for
myself such a grave sin?

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:16.170
Sorry! There was a mosquito!

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:17.290
A mosquito?!

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:18.750
See?

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.010
I see.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:21.670
A mosquito.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.340
Kana.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.430
Wh-What was that for?!

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:32.180
You ate my ice cream.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:34.980
This is great!

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:39.110
What's wrong with eating
my little sister's ice cream?!

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:40.570
What <i>isn't</i> wrong with it?!

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:43.700
But I gave you a winning
popsicle stick just the other day!

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:49.450
You think a 60 yen popsicle is comparable to a 280 yen, including tax, ice cream?

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.750
That's no excuse for violence!

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:53.790
There was a mosquito.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.170
A big one.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:58.590
That's how it goes.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.210
I see.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:01.090
A mosquito.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.460
Ninomiya-kun!

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:03.340
Sensei...

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:04.510
I wonder if Uncle Takeru's on vacation.

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:05.800
Ninomiya-kun...
I wonder if Uncle Takeru's on vacation.

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:06.260
He said he was on paid leave.

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:07.890
Sensei...
He said he was on paid leave.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:08.100
What's paid leave?
Sensei...

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:09.600
What's paid leave?

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:10.970
He doesn't have to work,
but he still gets paid.

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:12.310
Sensei...
He doesn't have to work,
but he still gets paid.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:13.060
Ninomiya-kun!
He doesn't have to work,
but he still gets paid.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:13.310
That's what my dad said, anyway.
Ninomiya-kun!

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:14.560
Sensei!
That's what my dad said, anyway.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.060
He's still getting paid?!

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:18.110
So Takeru's on vacation,
but he's got money?

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:19.110
Sensei...
So Takeru's on vacation,
but he's got money?

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:20.520
So Takeru's on vacation,
but he's got money?

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:21.030
Wow. That sure is the life.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.280
Sensei!
Wow. That sure is the life.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:23.650
Ninomiya-kun!
I'm gonna go rub his shoulders for him!

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:24.700
I'm gonna go rub his shoulders for him!

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:25.400
Sensei!
I'm gonna go rub his shoulders for him!

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:25.700
Sensei!

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:26.070
Uchida.
Sensei!

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:26.700
Uchida.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:27.870
Kana-chan?
Yonnomiya-kun?

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:27.950
Kana-chan?

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:28.490
When we went on a trip
.to the Minami household,

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:29.490
Sen... sei?
When we went on a trip
.to the Minami household,

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:30.580
Ninomiya-kun...
When we went on a trip
.to the Minami household,

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:31.790
I lost sleep because
you wouldn't stop talking.
Sensei!

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:32.830
Yonnomiya-kun!
I lost sleep because
you wouldn't stop talking.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:33.700
Sensei!
I lost sleep because
you wouldn't stop talking.

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:34.500
Ninomiya-kun!
I lost sleep because
you wouldn't stop talking.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:34.540
How will you make it up to me?
Ninomiya-kun!

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:35.460
Sensei!
How will you make it up to me?

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:35.830
Sensei! Sensei!
How will you make it up to me?

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:36.500
Our trip to the Minami household?
Sensei! Sensei!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:37.500
Ni—Yon—Ni—Yon—
Our trip to the Minami household?

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:37.540
Sensei! Sensei!
Our trip to the Minami household?

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:39.000
Everyone fell asleep
..while we were talking...
Sensei! Sensei!

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.920
Everyone fell asleep
..while we were talking...

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:46.220
I'm saying, without stripes, a zebra would just be a horse, right?

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:49.180
But zebras are white,
so they'd be white horses.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:52.260
Kana-chan, is this one going to take long?

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:55.140
No, it'll end when I feel sleepy.

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:56.770
Are you sleepy yet?

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:57.980
Not even close!

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:58.900
So, you see...

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:00.860
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:01.730
Wait!

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:10.700
Hey, nice stripes.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.540
You could at least listen until I get to a good stopping point.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.160
<i>You</i> were the one who
wouldn't stop talking!

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:17.750
I was sleepy!

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:18.790
Ow!

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.960
Why'd you hit me?!

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.750
There was a striped mosquito on you.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:28.970
Touma, you splashed me back
when it was raining, didn't you?

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:29.800
Huh?

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:31.890
Oh, you mean during the rainy season?

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:33.060
You still remember that?

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:33.560
Hi-ya!

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:34.180
Ow!

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.520
What was that for?!

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.520
There was a mosquito with
a fierce look in its eyes!

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:43.690
What's wrong, Touma?

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.030
Is there a mosquito on me?

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:46.900
N-No, there isn't.

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:48.200
Not on you, Yoshino.

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:52.660
Ow!

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:53.740
Hey!

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:56.290
Why, exactly, did you hit <i>me</i>?!

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:57.370
Well...

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:58.960
There was an impulsive mosquito on you!

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:00.250
An impulsive mosquito?!

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:12.510
There's a mosquito on you!

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:16.100
There's a mosquito running away!

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:17.680
There's no mosquito!

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:18.810
There <i>is</i> one!

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.310
There is a mosquito!

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:22.230
You just want to hit me, don't you?

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.270
Tell the truth!

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:25.820
If I do, will you let me hit you?

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:27.530
Not a chance!

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:32.870
She just smashed into Takeru!

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:33.910
You okay?

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:36.290
No, there was this...

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:42.120
huge, striped, impulsive mosquito with a fierce look in its eyes...

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:43.630
There was not.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:45.130
I knew it.

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:45.960
Huh?

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:48.130
Uncle Takeru fell asleep already?

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:58.140
A mosquito got him.

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:03.770
Man, Takeru's such a hopeless guy.

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:06.650
I don't want to grow up
..to be a grown-up like him.

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:08.280
Reiko-san...

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.900
I even made a reservation at the restaurant...

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:17.330
Kana, did he come to our place on his vacation because...

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:21.080
Let's be nice to him for today at least.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:22.210
For today at least.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.260
Good morning.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:39.770
It's not morning anymore,
but good morning.

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.640
One, two...

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:47.230
Morning, Kana-chan.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:48.480
Sorry for intruding.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:52.570
Is Takeru just hanging out here today too?

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:53.780
Seems like it.

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:58.080
Well, I gave him tea like a good host,
.so we can just watch over him warmly.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:01.750
Having him over every day is such a pain.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:03.080
I can hear you, you know.

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:05.620
So, where's Haruka-chan?

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:08.340
She went shopping.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:12.840
Where's my breakfast?

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:13.920
Nowhere.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:15.630
And my lunch?

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:16.640
Nowhere.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.300
Are you telling me to starve to death?!

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:20.350
Why don't you just
make something yourself?

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:23.430
I can't take this any longer.

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:24.890
I wanna eat right now.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:28.270
That's right...

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:32.230
The last time you were here, you ate the green soybeans that Haruka kindly provided.

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:34.490
Look me in the eyes!

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:37.660
Your adorable niece is hungry.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:40.120
As my uncle, don't you want
to do something about it?

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:42.410
I'm not your uncle,
I'm your cousin.

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:47.920
Your adorable niece wants to have lunch, even if it's only a tiny morsel.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.790
Why did you turn around like that?

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:51.550
Oh, no reason.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:57.300
Your adorable niece is Japanese, so seeing something turning makes her crave a rather specific food.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:58.840
Oh, Chiaki.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.050
What's this food you're referring to?

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:01.810
You know what I'm talking about.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.470
They go round and round.
Delicious Sushi Heaven
Seafood

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:04.810
Welcome.
Delicious Sushi Heaven
Seafood

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:08.270
Wow, I didn't think you'd
really treat us to sushi.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.860
Yo, Mr. Generous!

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:14.690
I guess we turned up at the wrong time.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:16.570
I'd say it was just the <i>right</i> time.

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:17.990
'Sup, Mr. Generous!

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:19.950
Sorry, Mr. Generous.

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:21.330
I didn't think we'd run into these three.

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:22.740
It's fine.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.000
It's fine, but...

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:27.160
1,000 yen per person.

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:28.250
Make sure you stick to that.

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:30.130
'Kay!

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:36.470
This place serves sushi on five types of plates, each priced between 100 yen and 500 yen.

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:38.840
Anything on a white plate is 100 yen.

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:43.140
If it's on a plate with a
fancy border, it's 200 yen.

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:47.930
This plate that looks kind
.of high-class is 300 yen.

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:52.940
This one with a deep and dignified feeling sets you back 400 yen.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:57.530
And anything on this gorgeously-patterned plate is a respectable 500 yen.

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:01.200
You can enjoy them all with 1000 yen,

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.120
but if you don't plan carefully,
you'll quickly go over.

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:06.200
Thanks for the explanation, Chiaki-chan.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.910
Excuse me, could I have two
plates of underbelly tuna?

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:10.040
Wow, impressive.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.130
Going for two 500-yen plates to end it right off the bat?

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:15.550
I got eggs, a tea-cup egg
custard and some salmon roe.

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:16.380
Eggs, huh?

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:17.960
Everything you got has eggs.

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:22.010
I don't know the name of the white thing I just ate, but it was really good.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:24.100
It was so chewy and crisp
and fluffy and melty!

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:26.100
There's lots of white sushi.

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:27.850
What on Earth did you eat?

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:29.060
Chiaki,

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:32.310
how about trading one of your sweet shrimp for my squid?

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.150
Sure.

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:40.700
So far, I've eaten one 100-yen plate,
one 200-yen plate, and one 300-yen plate

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.610
for a total of 300 yen.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:44.450
Hold on, Chiaki-chan.
Something doesn't add up there.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:46.240
You're a smart girl, right?

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:50.620
Touma, how about trading one of your scallops for my sweet shrimp?

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:51.710
Sure.

00:19:53.960 --> 00:20:00.010
So far, I've eaten two 100-yen plates,
one 200-yen plate, and two 300-yen plates.

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.220
I've eaten so much, but
I've only spent 500 yen!

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:04.340
Chiaki-chan, could you
try calculating that again?

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:08.520
Uchida, how about trading one of your salmon roe for my scallop?

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:09.730
Sure.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:15.230
Yoshino, how about trading your last underbelly tuna for my salmon roe?

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:16.360
Sure.

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:18.360
Kana-chan, you've really
worked your way up!

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:21.320
Delicious Sushi Heaven
Seafood

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:23.160
That'll be 7,000 yen!
Delicious Sushi Heaven
Seafood

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:25.870
Let's think about this a
.little before we go home.

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:29.660
I said 1,000 yen per person,
but our bill is 7,000 yen.

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.120
7,000 yen?

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:33.080
There are only six of us.
It should be 6,000 yen.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.580
Doesn't Chiaki's stack look a little off?

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:38.920
The last two plates are 500 yen each!

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:40.960
That alone is 1,000 yen.

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:43.380
Why didn't you follow the rules?

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:47.640
Have you forgotten a certain someone?

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:49.850
That's Fujioka's portion!

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:51.640
That's impossible.

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:55.690
The proof is right here
on his mouth. Leftover rice!

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.270
That's impossible.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:58.860
It was delicious!

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:01.110
Chiaki-chan...

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:03.650
It was delicious!

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:05.200
That's impossible.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:07.200
I'm home.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:10.830
Sorry, I bumped into Maki and Atsuko
.and ended up talking to them for ages.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.330
That feels great, Chiaki-chan.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:18.380
What a good girl.

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:19.800
I'll get started on lunch.

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:22.840
We already ate sushi for lunch.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:23.970
Sushi?

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:27.680
Takeru treated us. Too bad
you couldn't join us.

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:29.220
Where'd you go?

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.730
Haruka-neesama, don't tell me...

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:35.770
...you went to buy groceries for lunch?

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:45.900
Haruka-chan.

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:47.820
Want to go for sushi?

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:50.200
Sure!

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:25.710
The light in this refrigerator is really dim, isn't it?

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:27.420
The dim-isn't-it refrigerator.

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:28.760
The dim-inn'it refrigerator.

00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:30.720
The demonic refrigerator!

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:33.890
Next time: "Vegetables with Your Merry Friends on Your Day Off."

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:36.180
Thanks! We'll be here all week!
